# The Cessna 172P Skyhawk: glideslope's first aircraft, held to its handbook's
# figures (assets/figures/c172p.xml).
#
#   name TEXT...                 what it is called
#   model NAME                   its JSBSim model, in data/jsbsim/aircraft
#   start AIRSPEED_KT THROTTLE   a flight begun in the air: its calibrated
#                                airspeed, and the throttle that holds it
#   mixture-lever FULL_RICH_BELOW_FT
#                                its engine has a mixture lever, which the
#                                autopilot leans for best power - but full
#                                rich below the pressure altitude
#
# Its published figures, if it has them, are data/figures/MODEL.xml, and its
# selftest's log data/selftest/MODEL.log (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).

name Cessna 172P Skyhawk
model c172p
class light-aircraft
start 100 0.7
# The handbook's maximum rate of climb, figure 5-6: "mixture leaned above
# 3000 feet for maximum RPM".
mixture-lever 3000
# Her main tyres and brakes, for a wet runway's grip (docs/ASSETS.md):
# Cessna 172P Pilot's Operating Handbook (1980), section 8: 6.00-6 mains at
# 28 psi; single-disc toe brakes, no anti-skid.
brakes 28 none
